  "code": "2713",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"45\" data-end=\"377\">The <strong data-start=\"49\" data-end=\"73\">Cold Agglutinin Test</strong> measures the presence of <strong data-start=\"99\" data-end=\"131\">cold-reactive autoantibodies</strong>, typically <strong data-start=\"143\" data-end=\"161\">IgM antibodies</strong>, that cause <strong data-start=\"174\" data-end=\"223\">red blood cells (RBCs) to clump (agglutinate)</strong> at cold temperatures (usually 0&ndash;4&deg;C). These antibodies can cause <strong data-start=\"289\" data-end=\"322\">cold agglutinin disease (CAD)</strong> or be <strong data-start=\"329\" data-end=\"376\">secondary to infections or other conditions</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"384\" data-end=\"411\"><strong data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"411\">Purpose of the Test</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"413\" data-end=\"699\">\n<li data-start=\"413\" data-end=\"505\">\n<p data-start=\"415\" data-end=\"505\">To investigate <strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"462\">unexplained hemolytic anemia</strong>, especially if it worsens in cold weather.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"506\" data-end=\"699\">\n<p data-start=\"508\" data-end=\"699\">To help diagnose <strong data-start=\"525\" data-end=\"552\">cold agglutinin disease</strong>, <strong data-start=\"554\" data-end=\"600\">atypical pneumonia (Mycoplasma pneumoniae)</strong>, <strong data-start=\"602\" data-end=\"630\">Epstein-Barr virus (EBV)</strong> infection, or <strong data-start=\"645\" data-end=\"698\">other autoimmune or lymphoproliferative disorders</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (elevated titer)</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates the presence of cold agglutinins. May be associated with <strong>cold agglutinin disease</strong>, <strong>infections</strong>, or <strong>lymphoma</strong>. Higher titers (e.g., &gt;1:64) are more clinically significant.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative</strong></td>\n<td>Cold agglutinins not detected or present in very low, clinically insignificant titers. Rules out <strong>cold agglutinin-mediated hemolysis</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low-positive (borderline titer)</strong></td>\n<td>May be seen in healthy individuals or during mild infections. Usually <strong>not clinically significant</strong> unless symptoms are present.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
